    culturalInsight: { en: "Shirauo's appearance in late winter has long marked it as a seasonal herald of spring in Japanese culinary and poetic tradition, prized as much for its timing as for its taste.", ja: "晩冬に現れる白魚は、日本の食文化と俳句の伝統において春の訪れを告げる魚として長く親しまれ、その味だけでなく季節の到来そのものが価値とされてきた。", vi: "Su xuat hien cua shirauo vao cuoi dong tu lau da duoc coi la dau hieu bao mua xuan trong truyen thong am thuc va tho ca Nhat Ban, duoc coi trong ca ve thoi diem xuat hien lan huong vi." },
    chefTip: { en: "Handle shirauo as little and as briefly as possible between arrival and service — its structural fragility means excess handling, not poor sourcing, is often what damages the fish.", ja: "白魚は入荷から提供までの間、できるだけ手を触れず短時間で扱うこと。その構造的な繊細さゆえ、仕入れの質よりも過度な扱いが魚を傷める原因になりやすい。", vi: "Xu ly shirauo cang it va cang nhanh cang tot tu luc nhap den luc phuc vu — do do mong manh ve cau truc, viec xu ly qua nhieu, chu khong phai nguon hang kem, thuong la nguyen nhan lam hong ca." },
    keyTakeaway: { en: "Shirauo's near-transparent body and fleeting late-winter season make it as much a symbol of spring's arrival as a dish to be eaten.", ja: "白魚のほぼ透明な体と儚い晩冬の旬は、食べる料理であると同時に春の訪れそのものを象徴している。", vi: "Than hinh gan nhu trong suot va mua ngan ngui vao cuoi dong cua shirauo khien no vua la mon an vua la bieu tuong cua su den cua mua xuan." },
