    description: { en: "Learn about kisu, the mild, subtly sweet summer whiting best known for tempura but also valued as a gentle introduction to white fish sashimi.", ja: "天ぷらでよく知られる、繊細でほのかに甘い夏の白身魚キスと、白身刺身への穏やかな入門としての価値について学びます。", vi: "Tim hieu ve kisu, loai ca trang mua he vi nhe va hoi ngot noi tieng voi tempura nhung cung duoc coi trong nhu mon nhap mon nhe nhang cho sashimi ca trang." },
    goal: { en: "After completing this mission, you will understand what kisu is, its season and flavor profile, and why it serves as an approachable entry point into delicate white fish.", ja: "このミッションを終えると、キスとは何か、その旬と味わいの特徴、そして繊細な白身魚への入門として親しまれる理由を理解できます。", vi: "Sau khi hoan thanh nhiem vu nay, ban se hieu kisu la gi, mua va dac diem huong vi cua no, va tai sao no la diem khoi dau de tiep can voi ca trang tinh te." },
    content: {
      en: `Kisu, Japanese whiting, is a small, slender fish rarely more than twenty centimeters long, with a soft silvery body and a flavor so mild that it is often the very first white fish recommended to someone new to raw seafood. Its flesh is delicate and slightly sweet, without the pronounced oceanic character of oilier fish, and its texture is soft rather than firm, which is part of why it is handled with a light touch throughout preparation.

Kisu reaches its best condition in summer, when its flesh is at its most tender and its flavor most pronounced, though it can be found in markets across a wider stretch of the warmer months as well. It is one of a number of fish whose reputation rests more heavily on one particular preparation than on sushi itself: kisu is a cornerstone of classic Japanese tempura, prized by tempura specialists for how its delicate, fluffy flesh holds up inside a light batter without becoming tough or dry, and many people encounter kisu at a tempura counter long before they ever see it at a sushi counter.

At a sushi counter, kisu is usually butterflied open into a thin, wide fillet, and it is common for chefs to apply a light salt-and-vinegar cure similar in spirit to the treatment given to hikarimono, the silver-skinned fish family. This is done less to mask any strong fishy flavor, since kisu barely has one, and more to firm its naturally soft flesh just enough to hold together well as nigiri, while adding a touch of brightness that plays well against its subtle natural sweetness.

Because its flavor is so gentle and its texture so soft rather than assertive, kisu is often described by chefs as a good "introductory" fish: it asks very little of a diner unfamiliar with delicate raw seafood, offering a clean, faintly sweet taste with none of the stronger flavors that can be intimidating in fish like saba or iwashi. In that sense, kisu occupies a useful teaching role in a sushi meal, a quiet, unassuming dish that rewards attention rather than announcing itself.`,
      ja: `キスは体長20センチほどの小さく細長い白身魚で、非常に淡白でほのかに甘い味わいと柔らかい身質を持つ。旬は夏で、この時期に身が最も締まり味も乗る。天ぷらの代表的な種として広く知られ、多くの人は寿司店より先に天ぷら店でキスに出会う。寿司として提供する際は開いて薄く仕立て、光り物と同様に軽く塩と酢で締めることが多く、これは臭みを消すためというより、柔らかい身を軽く引き締め、爽やかさを加えるためである。癖のない優しい味わいゆえ、繊細な白身刺身に不慣れな人への入門的な一品として親しまれている。`,
      vi: `Kisu la loai ca trang nho, than mem manh, hiem khi dai qua hai muoi centimet, co huong vi rat nhe va hoi ngot, ket cau mem chu khong dai. Mua ngon nhat cua kisu la mua he, khi thit ca chac va dam da nhat. Kisu la nguyen lieu tempura kinh dien noi tieng, va nhieu nguoi biet den kisu qua mon tempura truoc khi gap no tai quay sushi. Khi lam sushi, kisu thuong duoc mo buom thanh mieng mong, va cac dau bep hay uop nhe muoi-giam tuong tu cach xu ly ca thuoc nhom hikarimono, khong phai de khu mui tanh (vi kisu gan nhu khong co mui tanh) ma de lam se nhe phan thit mem va them chut tuoi mat. Vi huong vi nhe nhang va khong ap dao, kisu thuong duoc coi la mon ca "nhap mon" ly tuong cho nhung ai moi lam quen voi sashimi ca trang tinh te.`,
    },
    culturalInsight: { en: "Kisu's fame in Japanese cuisine rests primarily on tempura rather than sushi, a reminder that many classic sushi fish also have entirely separate culinary identities elsewhere in Japanese cooking.", ja: "キスの名声は寿司よりもむしろ天ぷらによるところが大きく、寿司の定番魚の多くが日本料理の他の場面でも独自の存在感を持つことを思い起こさせてくれる。", vi: "Danh tieng cua kisu trong am thuc Nhat Ban chu yeu den tu tempura chu khong phai sushi, nhac nho rang nhieu loai ca sushi kinh dien cung co danh tinh am thuc rieng biet o nhung noi khac trong am thuc Nhat Ban." },
    chefTip: { en: "When curing kisu, use a very light touch with salt and vinegar — its purpose here is to firm the soft flesh slightly, not to mask flavor, since kisu has almost no fishy character to hide.", ja: "キスを締める際は塩と酢をごく軽く使うこと。目的は柔らかい身をわずかに引き締めることであり、味を隠すためではない。キスには隠すべき臭みがほとんどないからである。", vi: "Khi uop kisu, chi dung mot luong rat nho muoi va giam — muc dich la lam se nhe phan thit mem, khong phai de che dau huong vi, vi kisu gan nhu khong co mui tanh can che." },
    keyTakeaway: { en: "Kisu's gentle sweetness and soft texture make it the quiet, approachable fish that eases people into the world of delicate white fish sashimi.", ja: "キスのほのかな甘みと柔らかな食感は、繊細な白身刺身の世界への穏やかな入り口となる。", vi: "Vi ngot nhe nhang va ket cau mem cua kisu khien no tro thanh loai ca de gan gui, dan dat moi nguoi vao the gioi sashimi ca trang tinh te." },
